<p>I adore this. Doubly so after knowing why. &lt;applause&gt;</p>
<p>But&#8230;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Clef did his duty, emitting a dry chuckle, and sat in a creaking chair. In a moment, the young agent in the chair stood, thanked the man, and passed him a ten. He accepted it, smiled, and waved the young man on his way.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It almost sounds like Clef is sitting in the young agent's lap. Perhaps &quot;&#8230;sat in a creaking chair to wait his turn.&quot;? Also, Clef is the only other person referenced in this paragraph, making &quot;passed him a ten&quot; indicate he passed to Clef on his way out. Maybe substitute &quot;the barber&quot; for &quot;him&quot;.</p>
<p>+1.</p>

